            <ArticleTitle>Renal-Clearable PEGylated Porphyrin Nanoparticles for Image-guided Photodynamic Cancer Therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">1702928</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/adfm.201702928</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Noninvasive dynamic positron emission tomography (PET) imaging was used to investigate the balance between renal clearance and tumor uptake behaviors of polyethylene glycol (PEG)-modified porphyrin nanoparticles (TCPP-PEG) with various molecular weights. TCPP-PEG10K nanoparticles with clearance behavior would be a good candidate for PET image-guided photodynamic therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
